  id: Occipitalis_muscle
  partName: Occipitalis muscle
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The occipitalis muscle is located at the back of the head and is primarily involved
    in moving the scalp. It works in conjunction with the frontalis muscle to control
    scalp tension and positioning. '
  - Although its role in facial expression is minor, it contributes to subtle movements
    such as raising the scalp or assisting in ear movement in some animals. It also
    helps maintain tension in the scalp, which can indirectly support other facial
    muscle functions.
